					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-10614294#post-4450419</guid>
				<title>CSS tweaks</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-10614294/nobody-s-observations-on-arson-activism-and-mustaches#post-4450419</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 20 Dec 2019 08:25:37 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>stordoff</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>5909240</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>It might be worth tweaking this to not use spans for the fonts. The site style forces word-break: break-all on spans for narrow screens (like phones), which causes it to break text mid-word. This looks really odd for hand-written text.</p> <p>Example:</p> <blockquote> <p>&#8230;was definitely a bit inconvenient, but consid<br /> ering that it said a whole MCD facility&#8230;</p> </blockquote> <p>Adding:</p> <div class="code"> <div class="hl-main"> <pre> <span class="hl-code">font-family: '</span><span class="hl-identifier">Reenie</span><span class="hl-code"> </span><span class="hl-identifier">Beanie</span><span class="hl-code">'; font-size: 22</span><span class="hl-identifier">px</span><span class="hl-code">;</span> </pre></div> </div> <p>to .page (and getting rid of the spans) seems to work. ([[size 125%]] also resolves to a span, but that's only an issue on absurdly narrow screens).</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
